<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hafiz Rahmat Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1708–1774</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hafiz Rahmat Khan was a Rohilla Afghan leader who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilkhand">Rohilkhand</a> as regent for the sons of Ali Muhammad Khan after 1748, leading a confederacy of Rohilla chiefs from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bareilly">Bareilly</a>. He supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a> in 1761. He was killed in 1774 fighting the Nawab of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> allies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hafiz-rahmat-khan.jpg" alt="Hafiz Rahmat Khan" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Third_battle_of_Panipat_13_January_1761.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
